{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed. There were **three independent bugs**, one for each symptom — full details in `ANSWER.md`, which parts of the colleague's note applied included.\n\n**Cause 1 — Connect button 401 for everyone.** The SPA used `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">` — a full-page navigation doesn't carry the `Authorization` header that only the fetch wrapper sends. Now init is an authenticated **POST** returning `{authorize_url}` JSON (`server.py`), and the frontend POSTs then does `window.location.assign(...)` (`static/app.js`).\n\n**Cause 2 — Authorize step rejected with 400 since 2026-10-02.** `config.py` listed `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR` twice (`:READ` + `:WRITE`); Intervals rejects duplicated scope areas since `:WRITE` implies `:READ`. The calendar sync added the second duplicate. Scopes are now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` — each area once.\n\n**Cause 3 — Rivera's \"expired, reconnect\" after one hour.** The Intervals token response has no `refresh_token`/`expires_in` — the token lives until revoked. The backend invented a 3600 s TTL and the refresher pass killed the connection an hour later. Expiry/refresh machinery is gone; revocation is now handled lazily: first **401** from the API clears the token and surfaces \"reconnect\".\n\nAlso trimmed the token exchange to exactly `client_id`, `client_secret`, `code`, and added a `purpose` check to the signed state.\n\n**Verification:** ran the full flow against a local mock of Intervals.icu (via `INTERVALS_BASE`, removed afterwards) emulating the documented quirks — 13/13 checks passed, including: the old duplicated scope is rejected while the fixed one is accepted, no-auth navigation still 401s, connect → wellness 200, status stays connected with no fake expiry, revoke → 409 + `reconnect`, and a reconnect round-trip restores the connection.\n\nChanged files: `server.py`, `static/app.js`, `config.py`, plus new `ANSWER.md`."}
